<http://data.silknow.org/object/351ee703-ab8f-309d-9c33-2d600005a636>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "The ground is of white satin. The design is a development of that of the Italian 15th century velvets in which large leaf-like forms are detailed with conventional, symmetrical bunches of flowers. In this piece the leaf-like forms are separated by a frame-work of conventional flowers and leaves.  The design is woven with white, green, yellow, light brown, pink and blue silk.  Made up of many fragments."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/2b1ac521-5ac1-3991-87d7-e4593a035780> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "The ground is of white satin. The design is a development of that of the Italian 15th century velvets in which large leaf-like forms are detailed with conventional, symmetrical bunches of flowers. In this piece the leaf-like forms are separated by a frame-work of conventional flowers and leaves.  The design is woven with white, green, yellow, light brown, pink and blue silk.  Made up of many fragments."@en ;
